  "researchNotes": "1) Licence: 'hdbank' is on data/licensed-institutions.json (Giấy phép 0026/NH-GP). 2) Key finding: HDBank's public unsecured-loan page states max term 60 months, a limit of 12 months of net income and a document list, but NO interest rate and no VND limit; the only rate figure is the bank-wide average (10,4% medium/long term, from 01/07/2026), recorded as benchmark, so that product is not rankable. 3) The only real offered rates are for the card-linked 'vay tiêu dùng linh hoạt': 1,5%/tháng (6, 12 months) and 1,7%/tháng (24, 36 months), flat on the original balance, from an undated product sheet that looks internal, plus Oct 2025 T&C. Existing HDBank card holders only; excluded from ranking. 4) Gaps: no fee schedule specific to the unsecured loan; the credit fee schedule (Phụ lục 07; effective date not found in extracted text, another version applies from 03/06/2024) only gives a bank-wide early repayment formula (1,5%/360 per day early on the prepaid amount per period); no mandatory insurance information found; no age or income rules; no overdraft (thấu chi) page for individuals found (only generic debit-card terms mention a possible overdraft). HD Saison excluded as instructed. 5) Contradictions: card loan limit (50% of card limit, max 100 triệu in sheet vs 80% of card limit in Oct 2025 T&C); early repayment fee 4% (sheet) vs 'per contract' (T&C). 6) Surprising: the product sheet is an internal-looking submission published on HDBank's CDN; the Oct 2025 T&C file carries an MB form code (19.QĐSP - MB.01/TTT) although its text names HDBank; the credit-card interest range of 2,0%-3,0%/tháng is high. All figures read 2026-11-02.",
  "retrievedAt": "2026-11-02"
}
